      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/second-sons-leaders-livestreams-9.7022853?cmp=rss</guid>
      <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/1683ccc7-5d8d-4ea4-891f-13a8b652e839,1766162985508/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C2268%2C1275%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A group of masked men hang a banner on an overpass.' width='620' height='349' title='An image from the group Second Sons Canada shows a demonstration they held at an overpass in London, Ont. last month'/><p>In official posts, Second Sons Canada calls itself a “men’s nationalist club” and promotes a nostalgic vision of Canada. But on personal podcasts and livestreams, its leaders consistently espouse antisemitism, violent rhetoric, praise Nazi Germany and use racist slurs.</p>]]></description>
